# Host directory holding the media library, bind-mounted read-only into the
# container at /media. Copy this file to .env and adjust per machine.
#
# Raspberry Pi: the NTFS drive is mounted at /srv/mediadrive. The container
# gets the drive root, so every top-level folder on the drive is browsable
# through the API/UI, not just a single "media" folder.
MEDIA_HOST_DIR=/srv/mediadrive
#
# Local dev example:
# MEDIA_HOST_DIR=./media

# Optional: 256-bit key (64 hex characters) that enables transparent
# decryption of "<name>.enc" files. Leave unset to disable the feature —
# plain files keep working normally either way, and encrypted files simply
# won't decrypt (they list under their literal ".enc" name and download as
# opaque ciphertext instead of playing).
#
# Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
# ENCRYPTION_KEY=
